## Engineering rules

- Follow `{{FRAMEWORK_OR_ECOSYSTEM}}` conventions and the boundaries documented in `docs/architecture/README.md`.
- Preserve public APIs, data formats, routes, environment variable names, and deployment behaviour unless the task explicitly changes them.
- Keep changes scoped; avoid unrelated dependency upgrades and repository-wide formatting.
- Add or update tests for behaviour and boundaries affected by the change.
- Never read, print, or commit secret values. Treat `{{SENSITIVE_PATH_SUMMARY}}` as protected.

## Workflow

1. Inspect relevant code, tests, docs, and current memory.
2. Plan multi-file or risky changes before editing.
3. Implement in coherent slices.
4. Run focused checks after each slice and the full relevant gates before completion.
5. Update canonical docs, `.ai/memory/LONG_TERM.md`, and `.ai/memory/SHORT_TERM.md` when facts or hand-off state change.
6. Review the full diff for accidental behaviour, path, dependency, generated-file, and secret changes.

## Definition of done

Work is complete only when the requested behaviour is implemented, relevant tests and quality gates pass or limitations are documented, docs/memory are current, and the final diff has been reviewed. Never push or deploy unless the user explicitly requests it and the environment authorises it.
